    "result_text": "All tests pass \u2014 `BUILD SUCCESS` with the full suite green.\n\n## Summary\n\nImplemented the optional owner `email` field across the OfficeFloor POST/PUT pipelines and the persistence + DTO layers.\n\n**Contract implemented** (from `AcceptanceTest`):\n- Email is **optional** \u2014 a payload without it succeeds.\n- When present, it must be a **syntactically valid** address, else **400**.\n- Stored and returned **lower-cased**.\n\n**Changes:**\n\n1. **`openapi.yml`** \u2014 added an optional `email` property (`format: email`, `maxLength: 255`) to the `OwnerFields` schema, so the generated `OwnerFieldsDto`/`OwnerDto` gain an `email` field (and `@Email` bean-validation on the PUT path).\n\n2. **`Owner.java`** (entity) \u2014 added `@Column(name = \"email\") String email` with getter/setter, plus `email` in `toString()`.\n\n3. **`ValidateOwnerFields.java`** (POST validator \u2014 does manual validation, not `@Valid`) \u2014 added `normalizeEmail`, mirroring the existing `normalizeTelephone`: blank/absent \u2192 skipped; valid \u2192 trimmed and stored lower-cased back on the request; invalid \u2192 adds an `\"email\"` error \u2192 400 via the existing `OwnerFieldsInvalidException` handler.\n\n4. **`ApplyOwner.java`** (PUT path) \u2014 sets the loaded owner's email, lower-cased (null when blank), for consistency.\n\n5. **DB schema** \u2014 added an `email` column to `owners` in all four dialects (`h2`, `hsqldb`, `mysql`, `postgres`); the test profile is `hsqldb` (`ddl-auto=none`, so the column must be declared).\n\n6. **Seed data** \u2014 the `hsqldb` and `mysql` `data.sql` used positional `INSERT INTO owners VALUES (...)`, which broke once the column count changed; converted them to explicit column lists (`h2`/`postgres` already used explicit lists).\n\nThe MapStruct `OwnerMapper` maps `email` automatically by name (entity \u2194 DTO), so no mapper change was needed. Response GET returns the stored lower-cased value.",
